            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical observation on Ashi points Sihua needling method for treatment of acute soft tissue injury].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>753-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To observe therapeutic effect of Ashi points Sihua needling method for treatment of acute soft tissue injury.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The patients were randomly divided into a treatment group (n = 105) and a control group (n = 108). They were treated respectively with Ashi points Sihua needling method and routine needling method. Their therapeutic effects and safety were assessed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The cured rate was 79.0% in the treatment group, better than 65.7% in the control group (P &lt; 0.05); after treatment, the improvement degrees of pain, dysfunction and the total cumulative score in the treatment group were better than those in the control group (P &lt; 0.05 or P &lt; 0.01); the treatment group produced more quickly the effect with a shorter cured period as compared with the control group (P &lt; 0.05 or P &lt; 0.01).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Ashi points Sihua needling method is safe and effective for acute soft tissue injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
